sst_analytics_responses_by_month — Survey Landing “Survey Response Trends” chart (Recent Activity).

DE columns: ResponseMonth (Text, yyyy-MM), ResponseCount (Number)

Counts completed answer rows (excludes SURVEY_OPEN). Chart JS maps the rolling last 12 calendar months to these rows.



SELECT

    SUBSTRING(CONVERT(VARCHAR(20), r.LastUpdated, 120), 1, 7) AS ResponseMonth,

    COUNT(*) AS ResponseCount

FROM SST_SP_Survey_Responses_DE r

WHERE r.LastUpdated IS NOT NULL

  AND LTRIM(RTRIM(ISNULL(r.Status, ''))) = 'Completed'

  AND ISNULL(r.QuestionID, '') != 'SURVEY_OPEN'

GROUP BY SUBSTRING(CONVERT(VARCHAR(20), r.LastUpdated, 120), 1, 7)



After changing SQL: re-run each query activity (overwrite/update target DE), then refresh CloudPages.



TextPageNumber batch — one sequence per SurveyID + QuestionID (20 non-empty text rows per page).

PageNumber batch — one sequence per SurveyID (20 response rows per page, ordered by LastUpdated ASC).

Re-run PageNumber/TextPageNumber query and update SST_SP_Survey_Responses_DE when batch logic changes.



Survey Results reads course cards/chart from sst_analytics_per_course (TotalResponses, CompletedRespondents, UniqueRespondents, CompletionRatePct).



Detailed CSV export (server): same CloudPage with export=csv and surveyid (optional exportCourse when a course card filter is active). Loops PageNumber 1..max from SST_SP_Survey_Responses_DE; skips SURVEY_OPEN. Does not apply the table search box filter.



Detailed table course filter: course card click sets detailCourse on the URL (with view=responses and detailPage=1). Server loads matching rows across the full survey (not only the current PageNumber batch). Pagination keeps detailCourse on each page.



Survey Landing no longer Retrieve()s the full responses DE. It reads sst_analytics_per_survey (grid open counts + stat cards) and sst_analytics_responses_by_month (activity chart). Schedule the same refresh cadence as other analytics DEs.

Survey Landing Avg Response Rate (landingAvgResponseRate): for each row in sst_analytics_per_survey, rate = CompletedSurvey / OpenedSurvey (or CompletedSurvey / UniqueRespondents if OpenedSurvey is 0); then arithmetic mean of those rates, rounded to whole percent. Requires per-survey query refresh.


